1
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:08,360
<i>It hasn't even been a day,</i>
<i>and he's already made rules.</i>

2
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:11,240
<i>I've already created our</i>
<i>Instagram account. Go follow it.</i>

3
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:12,200
MINT - I LOVE YOU SO MUCH

4
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,960
<i>Cheating isn't funny.</i>

5
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:16,320
Now it's like
everyone is criticizing our club.

6
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:19,440
<i>From now on,</i>
<i>never date anyone close to you</i>

7
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:20,480
<i>if you don't want drama in your life.</i>

8
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:22,760
You're pretty cool.

9
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:27,640
- I bought you something.
- Thanks.

10
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:30,520
Shit, I posted it by accident.

11
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:33,440
Shit.

12
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:37,560
Good thing I deleted it fast.

13
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:43,120
Who are the three girls Ink's dating?

14
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:45,240
LeeIth. LeeIth.

15
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:46,400
What?

16
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:56,040
You're still awake, right?

17
00:00:57,080 --> 00:00:58,080
What do you think?

18
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:00,200
I figured you were.

19
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:04,840
You saw my story, didn't you?

20
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:09,080
<i>Should I say "yes" or "no"?</i>

21
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:13,120
<i>But I don't think</i>
<i>I can lie my way out of this.</i>

22
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:15,840
So?

23
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:19,760
I didn't see it.

24
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:21,640
Why?

25
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:25,280
Okay, you didn't see it, so never mind.

26
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:28,320
Wait, wait, wait.

27
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,160
You're acting suspicious.

28
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:31,880
What is it? Tell me.

29
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,480
I…

30
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:37,440
was just worried you'd get the wrong idea.

31
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:40,480
You'd think I have a crush on my friend.

32
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:42,440
Then you'd spread fake news.

33
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:43,840
I can't be bothered clearing it up.

34
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:46,520
I see. Then why did you post it?

35
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:48,720
The photo looked good,
and I liked the song.

36
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:49,960
Then why'd you delete it?

37
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:52,400
- I just wanted it up for a second.
- Three seconds?

38
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:53,600
Gen Z.

39
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:55,800
That's beyond Gen Z. More like Gen Beta.

40
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:58,280
That's all I wanted to say. Nothing else.

41
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:01,280
- I don't see a problem.
- See you.

42
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:06,920
You're good at everything except lying.

43
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:10,720
I'll find out who you have a crush on.

44
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:45,840
You're not usually this nosy.

45
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:50,080
I'm the club president.

46
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:53,440
What if you
and that person like each other?

47
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:55,080
Shouldn't I know?

48
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:02,160
Why are you making that face?

49
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,640
You don't believe me?

50
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:06,160
No, asshole.

51
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,640
The sun's in my eyes.

52
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:10,240
Come on, let's sit down.

53
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,720
Stop staring at me, asshole.

54
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:17,880
You can rule me out.

55
00:04:17,959 --> 00:04:19,959
I'm not that close to Ter.

56
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:21,839
It's probably not me.

57
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:28,960
And you're out too.

58
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:31,800
A friendly guy like Putter
would never like a jerk like you.

59
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,560
You're filthy.

60
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:35,720
And you're always picking fights with him.

61
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,000
Pass me some rice.

62
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:39,800
Fine.

63
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,640
You're acting weird.

64
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,720
You're not gonna fire back?

65
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:49,440
Something's off with you, LeeIth.

66
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:56,520
You think you can hide it
from your best friend of seven years,

67
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,400
who's known you

68
00:04:58,480 --> 00:05:00,680
since you were Pikachu-sized?

69
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,320
Seriously?

70
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:04,520
You…

71
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:11,040
Want to take a guess, asshole?

72
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,040
What's on my mind?

73
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:17,120
You want me to say it?

74
00:05:17,840 --> 00:05:20,360
Yeah. Don't keep me waiting.

75
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:24,640
I think…

76
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:29,440
you're just dying to know
his business, asshole.

77
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:32,600
You're such a troll.

78
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:33,840
You're putting on quite an act.

79
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:39,720
Shit, it's almost eight.

80
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:40,880
I've gotta go.

81
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:42,680
I need to see Ms. Aom.

82
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:45,600
Ms. Aom?

83
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:48,880
Yeah.

84
00:05:48,960 --> 00:05:51,520
Well, she wants to talk about my future.

85
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:54,520
Maybe I looked a little lost that day.

86
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:56,000
See you.

87
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:01,120
I don't even know her name.

88
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:02,720
Is she in the Arts program?

89
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:04,520
Or maybe a senior?

90
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:07,200
Who can I ask?

91
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:08,840
LeeIth.

92
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:10,600
You're here to see me?

93
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:12,080
Yeah.

94
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:16,480
Damn, perfect.

95
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:18,600
The right person, at the right time.

96
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:23,880
Hey, you guys.

97
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:26,320
- Can I ask you something?
- Go ahead.

98
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:29,000
Do you know these three girls?

99
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:31,560
Who do you think I am?

100
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,080
The first one is Eve.

101
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:39,000
<i>She's on the school sports team</i>
<i>and focused on athletics.</i>

102
00:06:39,080 --> 00:06:41,680
<i>She dreams of studying Sports Science.</i>

103
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:43,600
EVE GRADE 10 / CLASS 3

104
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:46,920
The next one is Momelon.

105
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,920
<i>She's a trainee under</i>
<i>an entertainment company.</i>

106
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,480
<i>But the company hasn't been revealed yet.</i>

107
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:53,680
<i>And… The last one</i>

108
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:55,240
is Padlom.

109
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:56,520
She's an old friend of mine.

110
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:58,400
But she's got a bad attitude.
Stay away from her.

111
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,040
No, no.

112
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:07,560
Do these three know Putter?

113
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:10,280
If Yihwa knows that much,

114
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:11,880
she's more than just nosy.

115
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:13,400
She should be a fortune teller.

116
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:14,640
Hey.

117
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:16,760
Yeah, true.

118
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:19,600
So, why are you asking?

119
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:21,920
Or…

120
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:24,400
Oh, it's nothing.

121
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:29,360
By the way, why don't you just ask Putter?

122
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:30,640
Aren't you in the same club?

123
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,320
Oh, right.

124
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:35,440
You guys are so smart.

125
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:37,560
Thanks. I've gotta go. Bye.

126
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:45,840
I think LeeIth and Putter
are totally real.

127
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:47,240
TerLee.

128
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:50,400
#LEEITHPUTTER
#TERLEE

129
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:54,200
After graduating high school,
what are your plans, Ithadon?

130
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:01,080
My family has already decided.

131
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:04,200
I'll probably study
engineering like my dad.

132
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:07,000
Sounds like your path is already set.

133
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:12,080
So why did you tell me that day
you didn't know what to look forward to?

134
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:19,560
So the truth is,
you don't want to study engineering.

135
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,160
You're spot on, Miss.

136
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,560
How did you know?

137
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:24,640
Are you a fortune teller?

138
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:27,680
More like a good guesser.

139
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:30,840
That's such a dad joke.

140
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:34,640
I studied psychology,

141
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:36,640
so I'm pretty good at reading people.

142
00:08:37,159 --> 00:08:39,440
If we understand the person
in front of us,

143
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:41,520
and the experiences they've been through,

144
00:08:42,039 --> 00:08:44,000
we'll understand a lot more.

145
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:49,040
Teenagers like you
all go through similar problems.

146
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:51,640
You're not the only one
who's been through them.

147
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:53,680
I've been there too.

148
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:55,880
Really?

149
00:08:57,720 --> 00:09:00,960
Actually,
I wanted to be a guidance counselor.

150
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:03,000
But my parents wouldn't let me.

151
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:05,960
So I studied psychology for them.

152
00:09:06,680 --> 00:09:10,760
But in the end,
I still got to do what I love.

153
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:15,200
At your age,
you're still discovering who you are.

154
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:16,920
Just go for it.

155
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:19,760
The things you like or dislike

156
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:23,560
might lead you somewhere unexpected.

157
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:32,800
Ms. Aom, an I ask you something?

158
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:36,000
Of course. Go ahead.

159
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:41,840
You're peeing like you're angry.

160
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:43,280
What got into you?

161
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:51,120
Hey, can I ask you something?

162
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:52,080
What is it?

163
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,360
After school,

164
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,840
where does Putter usually go?

165
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:00,520
Why are you asking?

166
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:04,640
I want to know how to read someone's mind.

167
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:08,640
To read someone's mind, first,

168
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:11,720
you need to understand their environment.

169
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:14,400
He's been prepping
for architecture school lately.

170
00:10:16,560 --> 00:10:17,760
He's so hardworking.

171
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:20,080
We're only in Grade 10,
and he's already preparing?

172
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:22,400
Everyone's preparing now.

173
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:24,080
They've all finished their portfolios.

174
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:25,400
You're the only one left.

175
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:29,600
Why does this feel so confusing?

176
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:32,160
People's hearts are so hard to read.

177
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,160
What are you doing here?

178
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:39,440
I'm here to study too.

179
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,360
You want to study architecture too?

180
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:42,560
No.

181
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:44,320
I just wanted to try something new.

182
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:45,800
Aren't you trying too many things?

183
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:47,480
Here, I got this for you.

184
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:48,400
It's your favorite.

185
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:55,200
Did you put something in it?

186
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:56,560
You never act like this.

187
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:59,080
We're roommates.
We should be close, right?

188
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:04,600
You're close with everyone
at school except me.

189
00:11:04,680 --> 00:11:05,800
Damn.

190
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:07,800
Isn't that kind of hurtful?

191
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:09,320
Are you pouting?

192
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:10,240
I thought that was just your face.

193
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:11,920
There you go, bullying me again.

194
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,160
Only because it's you.

195
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:19,160
Seriously,
I do want to be friends with you, but…

196
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:20,960
But what?

197
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:22,400
You're not very likeable.

198
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:25,880
The snacks aren't enough?

199
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:27,160
Not even close, buddy.

200
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:35,280
Second, spend more time with them.

201
00:11:39,960 --> 00:11:40,920
Nice.

202
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:43,480
If you're only complimenting my bag,

203
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:45,720
then buy it from me
and pose with it yourself.

204
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:46,920
Let's take some pictures.

205
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,280
No, I don't want to.

206
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:49,680
Come on.

207
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:01,600
Look. This plush is so damn cute.

208
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:12,400
Damn.

209
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:13,720
I won a plush.

210
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:16,680
It's for you.

211
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:18,920
Trust the king of fashion.

212
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:19,880
Get out of here.

213
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,680
I don't like owing people.

214
00:12:26,040 --> 00:12:27,840
How about this?

215
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:30,280
Here, this one's for you.

216
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:31,920
Now we're even.

217
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,560
Besides, that ugly-looking plush…

218
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:35,960
I'm not hanging it on my bag alone.

219
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:14,280
I'm back.

220
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:16,240
I got you something.

221
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:19,480
Thanks.

222
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:31,960
Why don't you just eat it whole?

223
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:36,160
And does chicken with strawberries
even go together?

224
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:38,720
Not really.

225
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:41,560
But cooking a whole piece
means using the kitchen.

226
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:44,000
We have a kitchen in our room too.

227
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:50,640
I mean… my room.

228
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:55,240
I just don't want to
make the kitchen messy.

229
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:01,640
Then… if I want to understand you,

230
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:04,920
I guess I should try drinking it.

231
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,240
<i>Third,</i>

232
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:10,320
imagine how you'd feel if you were them.

233
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:15,360
Don't force yourself if you can't.

234
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:22,120
You okay?

235
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:24,240
I'm fine.

236
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:28,000
Here, have some water.

237
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:29,360
Drink some. Wash it down.

238
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:40,920
Can I have some too?

239
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:48,800
Come on, let's go home.

240
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:51,080
Let's go.

241
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:04,960
Let's go.

242
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:21,280
That feels good.

243
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:26,440
Where are you going?

244
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:28,360
To take a shower.

245
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:30,360
You're such a clean freak.

246
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:32,960
I'm not. I'm just being considerate.

247
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:35,520
I don't want to lie on
the couch all dirty.

248
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:37,080
Come on, don't worry about that.

249
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:38,360
See? I'm already lying on it.

250
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:39,720
No.

251
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:42,840
Come here.

252
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:46,240
- Come on. It's fine. Hurry.
- Hey, no way.

253
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:49,960
Just try it.

254
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:55,320
So?

255
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:57,520
Mom's couch is awesome.

256
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:58,760
It's seriously comfy.

257
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:03,800
Do you usually watch movies?

258
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:05,920
Yeah.

259
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:15,120
How about we do something fun today?

260
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:22,120
And what exactly is "fun"?

261
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:32,560
This? This is your idea of fun?

262
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:34,520
Have you ever pitched a tent
and watched a movie indoors?

263
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:36,160
No.

264
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:38,280
Who does that?

265
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:40,200
I do.

266
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,080
You're such a dork.

267
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:49,360
Do you usually watch
movies, TV series, or anime?

268
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,040
I watch anime.

269
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:53,920
As for movies, I like superhero films.

270
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:56,840
Same here.

271
00:16:56,920 --> 00:16:58,280
You've got good taste.

272
00:16:59,240 --> 00:17:01,200
Here, pick what you want to watch.

273
00:17:02,800 --> 00:17:03,960
No, you choose.

274
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:12,480
I'm bored.

275
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:14,400
What should we watch next?

276
00:18:49,560 --> 00:18:51,680
You look so comfortable,
I can't bring myself to wake you.

277
00:18:57,880 --> 00:19:00,200
I'll even let you use my blanket.

278
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:03,520
I don't mind
that you haven't showered yet.

279
00:19:04,400 --> 00:19:05,400
So…

280
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:08,400
am I more likable now?

281
00:20:23,560 --> 00:20:24,720
Damn.

282
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:27,200
I fell asleep.

283
00:20:36,160 --> 00:20:37,240
You're awake?

284
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:39,040
Yeah.

285
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:42,200
Hey, don't come near me.

286
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:43,360
I haven't showered yet.

287
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:48,280
Yeah. You really stink.

288
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:51,440
Thought you weren't a clean freak.

289
00:20:53,560 --> 00:20:55,760
Hey, did you cook?

290
00:20:55,840 --> 00:20:57,000
Yeah.

291
00:20:57,920 --> 00:20:59,600
Wait here. I'll bring it over.

292
00:21:08,920 --> 00:21:10,560
Here. I made you a fried egg.

293
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:12,080
Way better than your strawberries.

294
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:15,120
Your likability score…

295
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:16,320
I'm giving you one extra point.

296
00:21:17,200 --> 00:21:20,080
That's way too little
for all the effort I put in.

297
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:24,440
Looks good.

298
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:25,480
Let me brush my teeth first.

299
00:21:25,560 --> 00:21:27,480
Wait, eat first.

300
00:21:27,560 --> 00:21:29,520
It's still hot. It'll get cold.

301
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:31,760
I made it just for you.

302
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:32,880
Okay, okay.

303
00:21:46,920 --> 00:21:48,160
What perfume are you wearing?

304
00:21:48,760 --> 00:21:49,920
I can still smell it.

305
00:21:50,560 --> 00:21:51,760
You've got a good nose.

306
00:21:52,720 --> 00:21:53,560
Were you sniffing me?

307
00:21:59,680 --> 00:22:02,320
No. Your perfume is just really strong.

308
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:05,160
It doesn't suit you.

309
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:09,640
I like it. I don't wear it to please you.

310
00:22:10,560 --> 00:22:11,800
Hurry up and eat.

311
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:14,400
Then shower and brush your teeth
so we can go to school.

312
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:16,040
Hurry up. Forget about eating.

313
00:22:16,120 --> 00:22:17,480
We're late.

314
00:22:17,560 --> 00:22:19,480
Come on, put it down.

315
00:22:20,040 --> 00:22:21,880
Yeah, go take a shower.

316
00:22:22,560 --> 00:22:24,000
- Okay.
- Go.

317
00:22:57,880 --> 00:22:58,960
Good morning.

318
00:23:07,560 --> 00:23:08,720
Good morning.

319
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:25,360
What are you doing here so early?

320
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:30,040
I'm here for a surprise inspection.

321
00:23:30,120 --> 00:23:32,120
I'm seriously at my limit, Mom.

322
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:37,240
I brought breakfast for Putter too.

323
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:39,760
Ter's already eaten.

324
00:23:39,840 --> 00:23:40,960
I made him breakfast.

325
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:42,560
Oh my!

326
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:44,560
I'll start the car.

327
00:23:44,640 --> 00:23:45,640
Putter needs to go to the hospital.

328
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:50,080
Mom! I'm your son.

329
00:23:54,040 --> 00:23:58,600
Putter, I brought a nice breakfast.

330
00:23:58,680 --> 00:23:59,880
Come eat with us.

331
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:02,200
Thank you, Ma'am.

332
00:24:05,400 --> 00:24:06,880
Such a respectful wai.

333
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:08,720
Such good manners.

334
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:09,640
You're so adorable.

335
00:24:10,320 --> 00:24:11,520
That's so unfair.

336
00:24:11,600 --> 00:24:13,080
I wai just as nicely, Mom.

337
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:15,040
It's not the same.

338
00:24:16,680 --> 00:24:18,600
Putter's kindness comes from within.

339
00:24:19,640 --> 00:24:20,640
I'm your son.

340
00:24:22,720 --> 00:24:24,840
Putter, let's go have some rice porridge.

341
00:24:25,440 --> 00:24:28,560
It looks delicious,
but I've already eaten.

342
00:24:28,640 --> 00:24:30,200
Have you had breakfast yet, Ma'am?

343
00:24:31,600 --> 00:24:33,120
Not yet, dear.

344
00:24:33,200 --> 00:24:35,200
Thanks for asking. No one ever does.

345
00:24:35,800 --> 00:24:37,440
Then let me help set the table.

346
00:24:37,520 --> 00:24:38,480
Thank you, dear.

347
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:40,400
Oh my. I'm so touched.

348
00:24:44,760 --> 00:24:46,440
Finally, I get to sit down.

349
00:24:46,520 --> 00:24:47,480
Someone did it for me.

350
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:49,720
Take notes from Putter, LeeIth.

351
00:24:51,760 --> 00:24:52,720
I've been sitting here the whole time.

352
00:24:52,800 --> 00:24:55,120
My own son hasn't even gotten me
a glass of water, Putter.

353
00:24:57,960 --> 00:24:59,800
Why don't you just adopt him?

354
00:25:06,640 --> 00:25:08,040
Then how about making him my son-in-law?

355
00:25:12,280 --> 00:25:14,760
I'll set Putter up with Lilly instead.

356
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:17,640
Oh?

357
00:25:18,160 --> 00:25:19,200
Or should I set him up with you?

358
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:25,640
Thai people will really say anything.

359
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:31,200
Putter, how's LeeIth at school?

360
00:25:32,920 --> 00:25:36,800
LeeIth is a really great guy.

361
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:38,320
Everyone at school likes him.

362
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:40,960
And Ms. Aom, our homeroom teacher,

363
00:25:41,040 --> 00:25:42,920
is very fond of him.

364
00:25:43,440 --> 00:25:46,520
He's also active in school,
especially in music.

365
00:25:47,360 --> 00:25:48,320
Hmm.

366
00:25:49,360 --> 00:25:52,920
If LeeIth is serious about it,
I'll support him.

367
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:54,320
I practice every day.

368
00:25:54,400 --> 00:25:56,680
In the morning, and again after school.

369
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:02,600
Putter, could you send me
a video of LeeIth practicing?

370
00:26:02,680 --> 00:26:04,240
I'd like to see his progress.

371
00:26:07,680 --> 00:26:09,520
We've never recorded one.

372
00:26:09,600 --> 00:26:12,880
Didn't you say you
practice before assembly?

373
00:26:13,920 --> 00:26:16,840
- Yes.
- Then play me a song this morning.

374
00:26:17,520 --> 00:26:18,480
Go ahead.

375
00:26:18,560 --> 00:26:20,480
I want to share it with LeeIth's dad.

376
00:26:20,560 --> 00:26:21,480
Come on.

377
00:26:33,080 --> 00:26:34,440
Shit.

378
00:26:34,520 --> 00:26:35,840
It's fully booked.

379
00:26:35,920 --> 00:26:37,400
Can we switch with them?

380
00:26:41,880 --> 00:26:44,320
That's the school band
competing in Hotwave.

381
00:26:44,400 --> 00:26:46,040
No way they'd switch with you.

382
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:48,240
What do we do?

383
00:26:50,160 --> 00:26:51,800
I ran all the way here.

384
00:26:54,840 --> 00:26:56,720
You just had to run your mouth.

385
00:26:56,800 --> 00:26:59,320
True. And you even lied to your mom.

386
00:26:59,920 --> 00:27:02,320
She said she wanted to support me.

387
00:27:03,560 --> 00:27:07,000
Oh. What about our homeroom?

388
00:27:07,720 --> 00:27:09,960
No. Too many people.

389
00:27:12,440 --> 00:27:14,560
- Hey, help me think.
- I am thinking.

390
00:27:17,320 --> 00:27:19,600
Why not use our club room?

391
00:27:20,200 --> 00:27:21,120
Good idea.

392
00:27:25,920 --> 00:27:27,200
Lazy Meow Meow.

393
00:27:27,280 --> 00:27:28,840
Meet at the club room now.

394
00:27:28,920 --> 00:27:29,880
Right now.

395
00:27:31,640 --> 00:27:33,760
Hey, I've got exam prep.

396
00:27:34,360 --> 00:27:35,840
Forget that for now.

397
00:27:41,160 --> 00:27:43,480
Damn. This is awesome.

398
00:27:43,560 --> 00:27:45,080
We totally nailed it.

399
00:27:45,160 --> 00:27:46,800
But there's one problem.

400
00:27:46,880 --> 00:27:47,960
We've never practiced.

401
00:27:48,040 --> 00:27:50,880
Since when are we called Lazy Cat?

402
00:27:50,960 --> 00:27:52,800
Lazy Meow Meow.

403
00:27:53,600 --> 00:27:54,680
Yeah, that.

404
00:27:54,760 --> 00:27:55,960
Oh, right. Guys.

405
00:27:56,040 --> 00:27:57,680
Can I ask you something?

406
00:27:58,440 --> 00:28:00,040
Please help me.

407
00:28:00,640 --> 00:28:05,160
I mean, maybe my mom will change her mind
and let me study music.

408
00:28:06,160 --> 00:28:07,120
Sure.

409
00:28:07,200 --> 00:28:09,040
- Sure, let's do it.
- We're in.

410
00:28:09,120 --> 00:28:10,040
I'm always ready.

411
00:28:10,120 --> 00:28:11,040
Indy.

412
00:28:11,560 --> 00:28:12,880
Looks like we'll have to
bring back our old songs.

413
00:28:14,080 --> 00:28:15,920
But we don't have a drummer.

414
00:28:19,200 --> 00:28:21,360
- Damn.
- Sheesh.

415
00:28:21,440 --> 00:28:22,760
I'm not messing around.

416
00:28:22,840 --> 00:28:25,040
Our group has got more than good looks.

417
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:26,800
We're total all-rounders.

418
00:28:26,880 --> 00:28:29,480
We're all total all-rounders.

419
00:28:32,040 --> 00:28:34,920
- That's awesome.
- Hold on.

420
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:36,720
Everyone's got an instrument.

421
00:28:36,800 --> 00:28:38,920
What about you, Tungtae?
What can you play?

422
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:40,880
I can't play anything.

423
00:28:40,960 --> 00:28:42,560
But…

424
00:28:42,640 --> 00:28:45,080
- Right, you're the only one left.
- I can probably…

425
00:28:45,160 --> 00:28:46,920
shake this.

426
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:50,400
- Enough, idiot. You're useful after all.
- Okay.

427
00:28:50,480 --> 00:28:51,320
- Okay.
- Got it.

428
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:53,520
Well, it suits you.

429
00:28:54,920 --> 00:28:56,160
We're ready.

430
00:28:58,280 --> 00:28:59,520
Here we go.

431
00:29:00,960 --> 00:29:03,120
Hey. Help me out.

432
00:29:03,200 --> 00:29:04,400
Mm.

433
00:29:05,360 --> 00:29:07,520
- Sure, I'll film it.
- Thank you.

434
00:29:08,120 --> 00:29:09,080
Come on.

435
00:29:09,160 --> 00:29:10,640
- Come on!
- Ready?

436
00:29:10,720 --> 00:29:12,600
- We're ready!
- Ready.

437
00:29:12,680 --> 00:29:14,200
- Go for it!
- Everyone's ready.

438
00:29:17,520 --> 00:29:21,240
<i>Someone once told me</i>

439
00:29:21,320 --> 00:29:24,920
<i>That on the day we find love</i>

440
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:30,280
<i>I would understand everything</i>

441
00:29:32,560 --> 00:29:36,280
<i>Then I met you</i>

442
00:29:36,360 --> 00:29:40,080
<i>And I felt this is even better</i>
<i>Than a dream</i>

443
00:29:40,160 --> 00:29:45,640
<i>It's truly wonderful</i>
<i>To have met you today</i>

444
00:29:46,640 --> 00:29:51,400
<i>The only problem is, I really don't know</i>
<i>If you feel the same way</i>

445
00:29:51,480 --> 00:29:55,160
<i>If I say it out loud, will I lose you?</i>

446
00:29:55,240 --> 00:30:00,600
<i>I'm scared that if I wait too long,</i>
<i>Someone else will win you over</i>

447
00:30:00,680 --> 00:30:05,320
<i>So today, I've decided to tell you</i>

448
00:30:05,400 --> 00:30:08,480
<i>It's just that</i>
<i>I've liked you for so long</i>

449
00:30:08,560 --> 00:30:10,600
<i>I've been in love with you for so long</i>

450
00:30:10,680 --> 00:30:13,760
<i>I want to tell you, I want to tell you</i>
<i>But I never have the guts</i>

451
00:30:13,840 --> 00:30:19,200
<i>I'm glad that today</i>
<i>You'll finally know that</i>

452
00:30:19,280 --> 00:30:20,800
<i>It's just that, it's just that…</i>

453
00:30:20,880 --> 00:30:22,880
What's that noise? What's going on?

454
00:30:22,960 --> 00:30:25,040
It's so loud.

455
00:30:26,400 --> 00:30:28,280
You're using the room improperly.

456
00:30:28,800 --> 00:30:32,040
You guys,
come with me to the disciplinary office.

457
00:30:32,120 --> 00:30:32,960
Come here.

458
00:30:38,240 --> 00:30:39,520
- Hurry!
- Quick…

459
00:30:41,640 --> 00:30:45,160
- Run!
- Let's go!

460
00:30:45,240 --> 00:30:48,080
Where are you going? I said stop! Stop!

461
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:49,960
Stop! Where are you going? Stop!

462
00:31:08,920 --> 00:31:10,760
Hello. Not me.

463
00:31:38,080 --> 00:31:39,520
You can relax now.

464
00:31:39,600 --> 00:31:40,880
The teacher's gone.

465
00:31:40,960 --> 00:31:43,080
Weren't you more nervous than me?

466
00:31:44,640 --> 00:31:46,080
Your heart's racing.

467
00:31:54,880 --> 00:31:57,320
Let's go. Time for class.

468
00:32:40,040 --> 00:32:41,200
Your mom looked happy.

469
00:32:41,880 --> 00:32:43,440
She really praised your performance.

470
00:32:43,520 --> 00:32:44,400
She said you had real passion.

471
00:32:45,400 --> 00:32:46,240
Are you being sarcastic?

472
00:32:46,320 --> 00:32:48,360
No, I'm not.

473
00:32:48,960 --> 00:32:50,680
You looked really cool.

474
00:32:51,360 --> 00:32:54,160
Cooler than I expected.

475
00:32:56,320 --> 00:32:58,280
That sounded weird, but thanks.

476
00:33:01,160 --> 00:33:03,160
I like people with passion.

477
00:33:04,280 --> 00:33:06,360
They've got drive. They've got energy.

478
00:33:08,080 --> 00:33:09,080
Really?

479
00:33:09,880 --> 00:33:11,240
Am I like that?

480
00:33:11,320 --> 00:33:13,000
See for yourself if you don't believe me.

481
00:33:20,120 --> 00:33:22,080
- This?
- Yeah.

482
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:27,280
See? Isn't it cool?

483
00:33:27,360 --> 00:33:28,520
Yeah.

484
00:33:29,160 --> 00:33:30,680
I'd like to watch you game too.

485
00:33:33,040 --> 00:33:38,520
I want to see you doing what you love.

486
00:33:50,000 --> 00:33:51,600
Time's up.

487
00:33:51,680 --> 00:33:52,800
Switch groups.

488
00:33:53,560 --> 00:33:56,120
Anyone who hasn't done the fitness test,
switch in now.

489
00:33:56,200 --> 00:33:58,280
Oh, right. It's our turn. Let's go.

490
00:34:27,280 --> 00:34:28,800
Sit wherever you like.

491
00:34:36,480 --> 00:34:38,159
I need this seat for gaming.

492
00:34:38,239 --> 00:34:39,080
Can you sit over there?

493
00:34:47,880 --> 00:34:50,400
It might be boring.

494
00:34:51,400 --> 00:34:52,679
That's okay.

495
00:34:53,199 --> 00:34:55,800
I want to watch you play.

496
00:34:56,840 --> 00:34:57,760
Okay.

497
00:35:04,320 --> 00:35:06,040
Hey, everyone. Ready for today?

498
00:35:06,120 --> 00:35:08,520
I've got a friend watching today.

499
00:35:08,600 --> 00:35:09,440
Cool?

500
00:35:09,520 --> 00:35:10,720
Hi, everyone.

501
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:15,320
Alright, let's get started.

502
00:35:17,120 --> 00:35:19,560
I've got my shield skill. Go engage.

503
00:35:36,240 --> 00:35:37,560
Swap. Done.

504
00:35:39,360 --> 00:35:41,080
Shit, that was cool.

505
00:35:41,600 --> 00:35:43,240
I'm gonna play one more match.

506
00:35:43,320 --> 00:35:44,400
You wanna watch?

507
00:35:45,600 --> 00:35:47,120
Sure.

508
00:35:50,360 --> 00:35:51,400
Let's keep going, guys.

509
00:35:52,560 --> 00:35:54,520
One more match. It's that easy.

510
00:35:54,600 --> 00:35:55,840
Let's keep it going.

511
00:35:59,560 --> 00:36:02,160
I LIKE THIS SONG.

512
00:36:08,040 --> 00:36:08,920
Do you know Putter?

513
00:36:09,840 --> 00:36:11,720
Putter? Who?

514
00:36:12,720 --> 00:36:14,160
Oh, you don't know Putter?

515
00:36:14,680 --> 00:36:15,480
MOMELON M.4/8

516
00:36:15,560 --> 00:36:16,760
Okay, thank you.

517
00:36:17,760 --> 00:36:19,440
- You know Putter--
- You're Yihwa's friend, right?

518
00:36:20,120 --> 00:36:21,600
Sorry, I'm not free to talk.

519
00:36:21,680 --> 00:36:23,200
PADLOM M.4/1

520
00:36:34,040 --> 00:36:36,320
Can I join you guys?

521
00:36:37,680 --> 00:36:38,680
Sure.

522
00:36:38,760 --> 00:36:40,000
We've got an open spot.

523
00:36:40,080 --> 00:36:42,800
But… there aren't any guys on our team.

524
00:36:42,880 --> 00:36:45,280
That's fine. I don't mind.

525
00:36:57,080 --> 00:36:58,160
Sorry.

526
00:37:00,880 --> 00:37:02,080
Do you need something?

527
00:37:04,600 --> 00:37:06,360
You just look familiar.

528
00:37:06,440 --> 00:37:07,600
I've got one of those faces.

529
00:37:10,120 --> 00:37:11,000
You're Putter's friend, right?

530
00:37:11,080 --> 00:37:13,440
We met at orientation.

531
00:37:13,520 --> 00:37:15,480
But are we friends? I'm not sure.

532
00:37:15,560 --> 00:37:17,520
I even replied to Putter's story,

533
00:37:17,600 --> 00:37:18,840
and he never replied.

534
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:22,920
Cut her out!

535
00:37:23,880 --> 00:37:24,920
What did you just say?

536
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:25,800
EVE M.4/3

537
00:37:25,880 --> 00:37:26,720
Hair…

538
00:37:28,160 --> 00:37:30,280
A haircut.
I've got a haircut appointment today.

539
00:37:30,360 --> 00:37:31,920
I should get going. See you, Eve.

540
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:33,040
- Sure, let's play again.
- Bye.

541
00:37:33,120 --> 00:37:35,600
Did those two younger guys come with you?

542
00:37:37,640 --> 00:37:40,680
They've been staring at you for a while.

543
00:37:41,280 --> 00:37:43,960
I don't think they were looking at me.

544
00:37:49,080 --> 00:37:49,960
You guys.

545
00:37:50,040 --> 00:37:50,880
Yeah?

546
00:37:50,960 --> 00:37:52,040
Ready?

547
00:37:52,120 --> 00:37:54,120
- Ready for what?
- Ready for what?

548
00:37:54,200 --> 00:37:55,040
Ready for what?

549
00:37:55,120 --> 00:37:56,360
Just be ready.

550
00:37:56,880 --> 00:37:58,840
- What?
- Hey, you two, come here.

551
00:38:00,480 --> 00:38:01,960
Hey, come on.

552
00:38:03,120 --> 00:38:04,280
Come here!

553
00:38:04,360 --> 00:38:05,560
You're so loud.

554
00:38:05,640 --> 00:38:06,880
I'll go over there.

555
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:08,320
Why so dramatic?

556
00:38:12,720 --> 00:38:14,400
Tungtae!

557
00:38:14,480 --> 00:38:17,280
Tungtae, I really like you!

558
00:38:17,360 --> 00:38:19,160
Neo, Leo.

559
00:38:19,240 --> 00:38:20,840
Neo, the twins.

560
00:38:22,080 --> 00:38:23,680
- Putter!
- What's up?

561
00:38:23,760 --> 00:38:25,120
- I like you.
- I know.

562
00:38:25,200 --> 00:38:26,920
I really admire you.

563
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:28,840
No, no. Sit down.

564
00:38:28,920 --> 00:38:30,360
Hand it over. Give me the form.

565
00:38:30,440 --> 00:38:31,440
- Hand it over.
- Here you go.

566
00:38:32,440 --> 00:38:33,920
- This is great!
- Yeah!

567
00:38:34,560 --> 00:38:36,480
- Can we sit here?
- Excuse us.

568
00:38:39,680 --> 00:38:40,760
Wait.

569
00:38:40,840 --> 00:38:43,440
These two middle school kids…

570
00:38:44,040 --> 00:38:45,800
- They remember us.
- They do.

571
00:38:45,880 --> 00:38:48,920
- You remember me?
- Yeah.

572
00:38:49,000 --> 00:38:52,000
They're the middle schoolers
who wanted to join our club.

573
00:38:53,120 --> 00:38:54,840
So, why do you want in?

574
00:38:54,920 --> 00:38:55,960
Go on, kid.

575
00:38:59,040 --> 00:39:00,800
- This clip. Look.
- Here.

576
00:39:00,880 --> 00:39:03,080
- Lazy Meow Meow.
- Meow Meow.

577
00:39:03,160 --> 00:39:04,880
- You were so cool.
- So cool.

578
00:39:05,560 --> 00:39:06,400
Let me see.

579
00:39:07,480 --> 00:39:08,600
He took my phone.

580
00:39:08,680 --> 00:39:10,760
Damn. It got so many likes.

581
00:39:11,360 --> 00:39:12,880
LeeIth, look.

582
00:39:12,960 --> 00:39:14,360
- Yeah.
- Let me see.

583
00:39:14,440 --> 00:39:15,480
Damn.

584
00:39:15,560 --> 00:39:17,120
How did it get this many?

585
00:39:17,200 --> 00:39:18,800
- Who posted it?
- I did.

586
00:39:19,880 --> 00:39:20,840
I posted it.

587
00:39:20,920 --> 00:39:22,840
- Really?
- I never miss good content.

588
00:39:24,640 --> 00:39:25,560
Master Tungtae.

589
00:39:25,640 --> 00:39:28,880
- You're amazing.
- You're awesome, Tungtae.

590
00:39:28,960 --> 00:39:33,880
To Yuki and me, you're our idol. My idol.

591
00:39:33,960 --> 00:39:36,440
You're the coolest boy band in school.

592
00:39:39,400 --> 00:39:40,800
I think they've lost it.

593
00:39:40,880 --> 00:39:43,400
Hey, calm down. Sit.

594
00:39:44,680 --> 00:39:46,280
We're the only band in school.

595
00:39:50,360 --> 00:39:54,400
Even if there were more bands,
you'd still be the coolest to me.

596
00:39:54,480 --> 00:39:55,520
Alright, alright.

597
00:40:01,160 --> 00:40:03,560
Okay, you two. Be honest with us.

598
00:40:04,240 --> 00:40:05,960
Why do you want to join this club?

599
00:40:06,040 --> 00:40:07,800
No hidden agenda. Just be honest.

600
00:40:07,880 --> 00:40:10,000
Sure. No problem.

601
00:40:10,080 --> 00:40:12,040
About you guys being my idols…

602
00:40:12,120 --> 00:40:14,600
I really mean that.

603
00:40:14,680 --> 00:40:16,280
But what I haven't told you is…

604
00:40:18,400 --> 00:40:19,840
I want to be popular.

605
00:40:19,920 --> 00:40:20,920
I want to be like you.

606
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:23,640
Just like this.

607
00:40:23,720 --> 00:40:26,600
I want girls all around me.

608
00:40:27,400 --> 00:40:29,120
I want to be like you.

609
00:40:29,200 --> 00:40:30,000
A man with a goal.

610
00:40:30,080 --> 00:40:31,760
Damn, just sit down.

611
00:40:31,840 --> 00:40:34,200
That's enough. I get it.

612
00:40:34,280 --> 00:40:35,960
Give me the pen. I'll sign him up.

613
00:40:36,040 --> 00:40:37,480
- Give me the form. I'll approve.
- Really?

614
00:40:37,560 --> 00:40:38,480
- Really?
- You're the best, Bro!

615
00:40:38,560 --> 00:40:40,600
- You're the best, Bro!
- Damn!

616
00:40:40,680 --> 00:40:42,360
Bro, gimme a kiss!

617
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:44,200
- Hey, calm down. Sit first.
- Bro!

618
00:40:44,280 --> 00:40:45,320
- The interview isn't over yet.
- Sit down.

619
00:40:45,400 --> 00:40:46,520
Yes, Sir.

620
00:40:47,120 --> 00:40:48,360
What about you?

621
00:40:48,440 --> 00:40:50,280
I want to be like you guys.
I want to be a rock star.

622
00:40:52,640 --> 00:40:54,320
- What?
- LeeIth.

623
00:40:54,400 --> 00:40:55,240
Do you see this?

624
00:40:55,320 --> 00:40:57,320
See what happens
when you're a bad role model?

625
00:40:57,400 --> 00:40:58,800
They're totally crazy.

626
00:40:59,400 --> 00:41:00,720
Aren't you a kid too?

627
00:41:02,800 --> 00:41:04,080
So, what do we do?

628
00:41:04,880 --> 00:41:06,680
- What about Yuki?
- Let him in.

629
00:41:06,760 --> 00:41:07,720
Take them both.

630
00:41:07,800 --> 00:41:09,520
- Do it.
- Let them join.

631
00:41:09,600 --> 00:41:10,720
- Come on, accept them.
- Yeah.

632
00:41:11,320 --> 00:41:12,880
Then welcome aboard.

633
00:41:12,960 --> 00:41:14,080
- Welcome.
- Welcome.

634
00:41:14,160 --> 00:41:15,800
Welcome.

635
00:41:15,880 --> 00:41:18,040
Can I finish first?

636
00:41:19,720 --> 00:41:22,240
Welcome to the Awkward Today,
Normal Tomorrow Club.

637
00:41:22,320 --> 00:41:23,880
Or, "You'll Get Used to It."

638
00:41:28,440 --> 00:41:29,760
- Shit, dude!
- Yeah!

639
00:41:29,840 --> 00:41:32,080
We've got recruits now!

640
00:41:32,160 --> 00:41:34,520
- Bro!
- Bro!

641
00:41:35,200 --> 00:41:36,080
Come on, let's go eat.

642
00:41:36,160 --> 00:41:37,560
- Bro!
- Take the juniors with us.

643
00:41:37,640 --> 00:41:38,640
I have a question.

644
00:41:38,720 --> 00:41:40,520
I'm in the club now, right?

645
00:41:40,600 --> 00:41:42,880
Can I use the club restroom?

646
00:41:42,960 --> 00:41:44,360
I really need to pee.

647
00:41:44,440 --> 00:41:45,280
Go, hurry.

648
00:41:45,360 --> 00:41:47,600
The juniors aren't shy, are they?

649
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:51,880
It's real chaos.

650
00:41:53,680 --> 00:41:55,120
By the way, where's Indy?

651
00:41:55,200 --> 00:41:56,560
Yeah.

652
00:41:59,000 --> 00:42:00,160
Speak of the devil.

653
00:42:00,840 --> 00:42:02,880
Looks like Indy's already in tears.

654
00:42:02,960 --> 00:42:06,600
<i>Why? Why me?</i>

655
00:42:07,840 --> 00:42:12,280
- Here he comes.
<i>- I'm doomed to be just a brother</i>

656
00:42:12,360 --> 00:42:16,160
- <i>Why? Why? Why?</i>
- <i>Why? Why? Why?</i>

657
00:42:16,240 --> 00:42:17,800
- <i>Why?</i>
- <i>Why?</i>

658
00:42:18,840 --> 00:42:20,040
Excuse me.

659
00:42:20,120 --> 00:42:23,640
Sorry, this is a BBQ restaurant,
not a karaoke bar.

660
00:42:23,720 --> 00:42:25,160
That's annoying.

661
00:42:26,520 --> 00:42:27,680
I'm sorry.

662
00:42:27,760 --> 00:42:30,040
Excuse me. Could we change tables?

663
00:42:30,120 --> 00:42:31,240
Of course.

664
00:42:36,880 --> 00:42:39,360
Hey, kid. I heard you got dumped.

665
00:42:40,520 --> 00:42:42,800
Anyway, I'm sorry.

666
00:42:44,600 --> 00:42:45,560
Shall we go?

667
00:42:48,720 --> 00:42:51,080
Keep it down.
You're disturbing the other customers.

668
00:42:51,160 --> 00:42:52,560
Sorry.

669
00:42:53,760 --> 00:42:54,960
Is Indy okay?

670
00:42:55,040 --> 00:42:58,640
By the way, Faye stood you up.

671
00:42:58,720 --> 00:43:00,360
Did it really hit you that hard?

672
00:43:00,440 --> 00:43:02,000
Tell us the truth.

673
00:43:03,960 --> 00:43:05,960
He's about to. Come here.

674
00:43:06,040 --> 00:43:06,960
Hurry up.

675
00:43:08,320 --> 00:43:09,240
Alright.

676
00:43:09,760 --> 00:43:13,360
She said she cares about me,
but only as a junior.

677
00:43:16,400 --> 00:43:18,120
Let's pull an all-nighter.

678
00:43:18,200 --> 00:43:19,640
Let's keep going.

679
00:43:20,800 --> 00:43:22,160
Let's go.

680
00:43:22,240 --> 00:43:25,120
- It's hot.
- Get us some water.

681
00:43:25,200 --> 00:43:26,360
- Get some water.
- I need water. It's hot.

682
00:43:26,440 --> 00:43:28,800
- Hot water.
- Hot water?

683
00:43:28,880 --> 00:43:30,000
- Our friend's heartbroken.
- Have some ice.

684
00:43:30,080 --> 00:43:31,480
Let's do this.

685
00:43:31,560 --> 00:43:33,040
So, where are we going?

686
00:43:34,360 --> 00:43:36,040
- To LeeIth's room.
- Hey.

687
00:43:36,120 --> 00:43:37,320
I'm in.

688
00:43:38,080 --> 00:43:39,680
- Hey, wait.
- What do you think?

689
00:43:39,760 --> 00:43:41,600
Did you even ask for my consent?

690
00:43:42,640 --> 00:43:45,440
- Let's just crash here.
- Finally.

691
00:43:47,360 --> 00:43:48,960
The sound's getting out. Keep it down.

692
00:43:49,040 --> 00:43:51,320
- It's too loud.
- It's not that bad.

693
00:43:51,400 --> 00:43:53,160
- Go, go.
- LeeIth.

694
00:43:53,240 --> 00:43:54,280
Come on, do it.

695
00:43:54,360 --> 00:43:55,800
Come on, nail it!

696
00:43:55,880 --> 00:43:57,600
Won't the building manager complain?

697
00:43:57,680 --> 00:43:59,040
I stuffed the gaps with towels.

698
00:43:59,120 --> 00:44:01,000
- Try again.
- Play it right.

699
00:44:01,080 --> 00:44:01,920
The sound won't leak out.

700
00:44:02,440 --> 00:44:04,280
Go, Go!

701
00:44:04,360 --> 00:44:05,640
Hang on.

702
00:44:06,560 --> 00:44:07,600
Hey.

703
00:44:07,680 --> 00:44:08,880
Let's have red soda.

704
00:44:08,960 --> 00:44:10,200
Pour me a glass.

705
00:44:10,280 --> 00:44:11,920
- Pour your own.
- You do it.

706
00:44:12,000 --> 00:44:12,960
The snacks are here.

707
00:44:13,040 --> 00:44:13,880
Hey, hey.

708
00:44:13,960 --> 00:44:14,920
I'm having some too.

709
00:44:15,440 --> 00:44:16,800
There's this too.

710
00:44:16,880 --> 00:44:18,800
- It's here.
- It's over.

711
00:44:18,880 --> 00:44:20,760
- Wanna play?
- Stop gaming already.

712
00:44:20,840 --> 00:44:22,880
- Let's do something fun.
- I'm in.

713
00:44:22,960 --> 00:44:24,800
- Okay, give me a sec.
- Come on.

714
00:44:24,880 --> 00:44:25,880
Yeah.

715
00:44:25,960 --> 00:44:28,000
You're so done.

716
00:44:28,080 --> 00:44:29,480
The guitar.

717
00:44:30,200 --> 00:44:31,800
- Karaoke?
- Let's do it.

718
00:44:58,320 --> 00:45:00,400
- Awesome!
- Awesome, Bro!

719
00:45:00,480 --> 00:45:02,240
That was amazing, man.

720
00:45:02,320 --> 00:45:03,600
- Really?
- Yeah.

721
00:45:03,680 --> 00:45:07,000
Seriously. That was so much fun.

722
00:45:08,200 --> 00:45:09,160
My bro's totally wasted.

723
00:45:10,760 --> 00:45:13,400
But LeeIth, you've got talent.

724
00:45:15,200 --> 00:45:16,960
- Seriously.
- Honestly,

725
00:45:18,080 --> 00:45:20,000
I had a dream too.

726
00:45:21,720 --> 00:45:24,520
When I was a kid, I loved rock music.

727
00:45:25,160 --> 00:45:26,560
I wanted to be cool.

728
00:45:27,960 --> 00:45:32,200
But my mom made me think
it was just a dream or a hobby.

729
00:45:35,680 --> 00:45:39,120
LeeIth. I get you.

730
00:45:39,200 --> 00:45:42,520
When we were kids,
we wanted to play for the national team.

731
00:45:43,040 --> 00:45:45,960
Yeah. But our dad wouldn't let us play.

732
00:45:46,040 --> 00:45:47,800
So we only got to play for fun.

733
00:45:48,600 --> 00:45:49,480
Yeah.

734
00:45:53,280 --> 00:45:55,000
I feel you, Bro. I get you.

735
00:45:59,160 --> 00:46:02,880
Honestly, I wanted to be an actor.

736
00:46:03,800 --> 00:46:06,720
But it was probably beyond my abilities.

737
00:46:06,800 --> 00:46:07,920
So I started my channel.

738
00:46:08,000 --> 00:46:09,800
It's the closest I can get.

739
00:46:13,800 --> 00:46:15,800
Wow, same here.

740
00:46:20,000 --> 00:46:21,840
Almost everyone's shared. What about you?

741
00:46:22,920 --> 00:46:24,680
Skip me. I don't have a dream.

742
00:46:24,760 --> 00:46:26,560
I just want a girlfriend.

743
00:46:27,560 --> 00:46:28,680
Ouch!

744
00:46:28,760 --> 00:46:32,120
- I get it.
- But… But…

745
00:46:32,200 --> 00:46:33,720
it's already over.

746
00:46:35,200 --> 00:46:37,400
- Aw!
- Ouch!

747
00:46:37,480 --> 00:46:40,520
- That's brutal.
- I feel you.

748
00:46:41,840 --> 00:46:42,840
That got sad fast.

749
00:46:42,920 --> 00:46:45,920
Let's just go home.

750
00:46:47,040 --> 00:46:48,600
Putter, what about you?

751
00:46:54,680 --> 00:46:55,800
This is so damn stressful.

752
00:47:02,400 --> 00:47:04,920
My dream is to become an esports player.

753
00:47:06,040 --> 00:47:10,120
As for architecture,
it's a career I can actually pursue.

754
00:47:11,040 --> 00:47:12,160
And it'll make my family happy.

755
00:47:13,320 --> 00:47:17,000
But if I had to choose,
it would be esports.

756
00:47:18,400 --> 00:47:19,680
I feel you, man.

757
00:47:19,760 --> 00:47:21,320
Alright, everyone. Together.

758
00:47:25,640 --> 00:47:28,240
Come on, everyone.

759
00:47:28,320 --> 00:47:31,560
Tonight, let's have the best time.

760
00:47:32,160 --> 00:47:36,360
To our dreams,
whether they come true or not.

761
00:47:36,440 --> 00:47:37,360
Who knows?

762
00:47:38,160 --> 00:47:40,480
- Come on, everyone.
- Cheers!

763
00:47:40,560 --> 00:47:43,000
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

764
00:48:10,160 --> 00:48:12,200
You lost. I won.

765
00:48:13,520 --> 00:48:15,360
Indy, switch with me.

766
00:48:15,440 --> 00:48:16,600
You tired already?

767
00:48:16,680 --> 00:48:18,400
The weak lose.

768
00:48:18,480 --> 00:48:19,960
- Bring it on.
- Think you're so good?

769
00:48:22,800 --> 00:48:23,880
You're not playing?

770
00:48:24,560 --> 00:48:25,520
Nah.

771
00:48:31,120 --> 00:48:32,720
Here, water.

772
00:48:34,600 --> 00:48:35,680
Thanks.

773
00:48:40,040 --> 00:48:41,240
Damn.

774
00:48:41,320 --> 00:48:44,560
We didn't even drink alcohol,
and it's still a total mess.

775
00:48:44,640 --> 00:48:45,920
I can already picture it.

776
00:48:47,200 --> 00:48:50,360
After they leave,
we'll be cleaning until we drop.

777
00:48:55,040 --> 00:48:59,280
Honestly, if I lived alone,
I'd leave all the trash lying around.

778
00:49:00,080 --> 00:49:01,800
But I don't want to inconvenience you.

779
00:49:02,400 --> 00:49:03,880
Living together means making compromises.

780
00:49:06,320 --> 00:49:07,240
Am I too strict?

781
00:49:09,080 --> 00:49:10,160
No.

782
00:49:10,240 --> 00:49:12,360
You're just so tidy I feel bad.

783
00:49:13,040 --> 00:49:15,360
Hey, you lost. See?

784
00:49:15,440 --> 00:49:18,040
No cheating.
You lost, so do five push-ups.

785
00:49:18,120 --> 00:49:19,320
Cut the heartbroken guy some slack.

786
00:49:19,400 --> 00:49:22,280
- I already went easy on you.
- Hey, Junior.

787
00:49:30,760 --> 00:49:31,880
Hey.

788
00:49:33,240 --> 00:49:34,800
Have you ever had your heart
broken like Indy?

789
00:49:36,600 --> 00:49:39,200
You always ask stuff out of nowhere.

790
00:49:40,400 --> 00:49:41,360
What?

791
00:49:41,440 --> 00:49:44,200
I'm an artist. I follow my feelings.

792
00:49:44,280 --> 00:49:45,920
Yes, Mr. Artist.

793
00:49:47,960 --> 00:49:49,240
You can answer.

794
00:49:50,440 --> 00:49:51,760
I won't make fun of you.

795
00:49:54,160 --> 00:49:55,000
Never.

796
00:49:56,040 --> 00:49:57,000
But…

797
00:49:58,080 --> 00:49:59,320
I do have a crush.

798
00:50:00,480 --> 00:50:01,920
Hey, what are you two talking about?

799
00:50:02,000 --> 00:50:03,200
Nothing.

800
00:50:03,280 --> 00:50:04,960
Hey, Putter and LeeIth

801
00:50:05,040 --> 00:50:06,480
are talking about their crushes.

802
00:50:06,560 --> 00:50:07,400
Let's go hear them.

803
00:50:07,480 --> 00:50:08,880
Damn, let me hear too.

804
00:50:09,520 --> 00:50:10,720
Yeah, let me hear.

805
00:50:10,800 --> 00:50:13,520
Don't keep flirting by yourselves.

806
00:50:14,640 --> 00:50:16,600
Come on, just tell us.

807
00:50:16,680 --> 00:50:19,480
This is a safe space.

808
00:50:21,040 --> 00:50:22,000
Yeah, right.

809
00:50:22,080 --> 00:50:23,800
I don't feel safe at all.

810
00:50:25,680 --> 00:50:27,400
That stings.

811
00:50:27,480 --> 00:50:30,320
- I feel you.
- Oh, buddy.

812
00:50:30,400 --> 00:50:31,240
Wait.

813
00:50:33,080 --> 00:50:34,280
Putter.

814
00:50:35,320 --> 00:50:36,720
You can give us a hint.

815
00:50:36,800 --> 00:50:38,120
Yeah, just give us a hint.

816
00:50:38,200 --> 00:50:39,240
If you don't want to say it.

817
00:50:41,200 --> 00:50:43,040
- Tell us!
- Tell us!

818
00:50:43,120 --> 00:50:44,840
- Tell us!
- Tell us!

819
00:50:44,920 --> 00:50:47,680
- Tell us!
- Tell us!

820
00:50:51,600 --> 00:50:53,400
The person I like…

821
00:51:01,720 --> 00:51:02,560
isn't here.

822
00:51:05,160 --> 00:51:06,560
What a letdown.

823
00:51:07,080 --> 00:51:09,000
That hint was way too vague.

824
00:51:09,080 --> 00:51:11,040
It obviously wasn't anyone here.

825
00:51:12,960 --> 00:51:15,880
What? I'm open to any gender.

826
00:51:15,960 --> 00:51:18,480
It's just that my type isn't in this club.

827
00:51:21,400 --> 00:51:23,520
Yeah. True.

828
00:51:27,600 --> 00:51:28,720
Move aside.

829
00:51:30,600 --> 00:51:31,600
What?

830
00:51:38,800 --> 00:51:40,280
For the peace of this club.

831
00:51:49,160 --> 00:51:50,600
Done. Our new rule.

832
00:51:50,680 --> 00:51:53,560
No dating anyone in the club.

833
00:51:53,640 --> 00:51:55,680
Break it, and you're out.

834
00:51:58,200 --> 00:51:59,720
Then you won't end up hurt like me.

835
00:52:06,000 --> 00:52:07,240
I'm safe anyway.

836
00:52:07,320 --> 00:52:10,400
I'd never have a crush on any of you.

837
00:52:10,480 --> 00:52:12,200
- Count me in too.
- Right.

838
00:52:12,800 --> 00:52:15,080
Hey. Someone take a picture.

839
00:52:15,160 --> 00:52:16,680
I'll do it.

840
00:52:16,760 --> 00:52:18,440
- Okay.
- I set the timer for 10 seconds.

841
00:52:19,000 --> 00:52:20,960
- Come on, everyone.
- Hold on.

842
00:52:23,000 --> 00:52:23,960
Ten.

843
00:52:24,560 --> 00:52:25,880
Nine.

844
00:52:25,960 --> 00:52:27,560
- Hurry!
- Eight.

845
00:52:27,640 --> 00:52:28,760
- Seven.
- Do this pose.

846
00:52:28,840 --> 00:52:30,600
- Okay, come on.
- No heart pose!

847
00:52:30,680 --> 00:52:32,120
- Five.
- No, no!

848
00:52:32,200 --> 00:52:33,200
Four.

849
00:52:33,720 --> 00:52:34,880
- Three.
- Damn.

850
00:52:34,960 --> 00:52:35,880
Two.

851
00:52:35,960 --> 00:52:38,120
- Watch out!
- Hey!

852
00:52:44,680 --> 00:52:47,880
<i>If I were you,</i>
<i>I'd probably think you felt the same way.</i>

853
00:52:48,400 --> 00:52:49,840
<i>But I guess you don't.</i>

854
00:53:14,520 --> 00:53:16,360
<i>You guys are roommates. I don't mind that.</i>

855
00:53:16,440 --> 00:53:17,800
But you're not dating, right?

856
00:53:17,880 --> 00:53:20,280
<i>This week's club mission is helping Indy.</i>

857
00:53:20,360 --> 00:53:21,440
The love you chase slips away,

858
00:53:21,520 --> 00:53:23,720
but the love you never looked for
is right beside you.

859
00:53:23,800 --> 00:53:25,520
<i>Someone's about to confess.</i>

860
00:53:25,600 --> 00:53:27,000
<i>Don't lose to the voice in your head.</i>

861
00:53:27,080 --> 00:53:27,960
<i>I made that rule myself.</i>

862
00:53:28,040 --> 00:53:31,200
What inspired you to confess to Summer?

863
00:53:31,280 --> 00:53:33,480
<i>It may sound cliche, but…</i>

864
00:53:33,560 --> 00:53:34,640
<i>I'd regret it if I never told her.</i>

865
00:53:35,240 --> 00:53:37,400
<i>Thank you for always looking after me,</i>

866
00:53:37,480 --> 00:53:40,520
<i>caring about me,</i>
<i>and making me feel so comfortable.</i>

867
00:53:40,600 --> 00:53:42,000
<i>I want to tell you…</i>
